## Interfaces reimplemented from public documentation

omt interoperates with software it does not include and is not derived from.
The following are *interfaces* — escape-sequence numbers, wire protocols, file
formats and configuration schemas — reimplemented from their public
documentation so that files and sessions written for other tools work here.
No code from any of them is included, adapted or translated.

- Terminal escape sequences: the ECMA-48 / xterm control-sequence set, OSC 7
  (working directory), OSC 8 (hyperlinks), OSC 52 (clipboard), OSC 133 (shell
  integration), OSC 1337 (user variables), and DEC private modes.
- Theme and settings file formats: YAML theme schemas, flat JSON settings, and
  the `.itermcolors` property-list key names.
- Agent protocols: the Agent Client Protocol, per-agent app-server JSON-RPC
  methods, hook payload schemas, and agent transcript formats. Where a vendor
  ships generated bindings for its own protocol, those bindings were read as
  documentation.

See `docs/architecture/14-licensing.md` for the policy this follows, including
which licence classes constrain what omt may take.

## Third-party dependencies

Rust dependencies are declared in `Cargo.toml` and their licences are recorded
in `Cargo.lock`; run `cargo license` or `cargo about` for the resolved list.
The web client vendors nothing: `web/package.json` has no runtime dependencies,
and the browser client ships as the TypeScript in this repository compiled to
JavaScript.
